+# Daily Grind homepage analytics
+
+`index.html` loads `analytics.js` with `defer`. It records one `page_view` on
+initialization (and each back/forward cache restoration), plus delegated `click`
+events, including clicks on nested elements inside links and buttons. Tracking
+does not prevent or delay the default click action.
+
+Configure `ENDPOINT` in `analytics.js` for your collector. The default is
+`POST /api/analytics`; this static site does **not** implement that receiving
+endpoint. The collector must accept JSON with this shape and return a successful
+HTTP status (for example, `204`):
+
+```json
+{
+  "events": [
+    { "type": "page_view", "page": "/", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z" },
+    { "type": "click", "tag": "a", "target": "a", "destination": "/menu", "page": "/", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.500Z" }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Click targets use `data-analytics`, then the element ID, then its tag name.
+Same-origin links also include their destination path. No element text, input
+values, query strings, or URL fragments are collected.
+
+Events coalesce until one second passes without another event, with a maximum
+wait of ten seconds during sustained interaction. Supported browsers use
+`fetchLater()` and cancel/replace the pending request as the batch grows. Other
+browsers use a timer and flush on page hiding or departure with `sendBeacon()`,
+falling back to a low-priority `fetch()` with `keepalive` if necessary. Native
+API errors also switch to this fallback.
+
+Batches flush at 50 events or before exceeding 48 KiB of UTF-8 JSON to stay below
+the shared browser deferred-request quota. Delivery is best effort: there is no
+persistent storage or automatic retry, and failures never block site interaction.
+An activated deferred request is not an acknowledgment from the collector.
